WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.036
Some new developments out of

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.170
Ukraine this morning

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:04.771
where officials

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.873
say the counteroffensive in Luhansk

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.108
is progressing.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.142
Ukrainian forces

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:10.944
now controlling a key highway

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.178
in that region,

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.613
bombarding the important

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:14.914
Russian supply route,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.649
leaving it unusable.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.451
Meantime, Russia is responding

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.185
to the counter

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.054
offensive a top Russian official

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.288
threatening to hold Kiev's

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.657
electricity supply hostage,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.126
saying power would be restored

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.294
only if Ukraine recognizes

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.764
Russia's attempted annexation.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:31.531
Let's get some insight

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.332
now from retired

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.100
Lieutenant General Mark Hertling.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.735
He's a CNN military analyst

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.104
and a former commanding general for U.S.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.440
Army, Europe and Seventh Army General,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.007
good morning

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.909
and thanks for being with us.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.643
The Kremlin

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.645
threatening to take Kiev's power

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.447
supply hostage.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.183
How seriously do you take that threat

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.919
It would certainly have a huge effect

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.387
on the nation of Ukraine, Boris.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.488
And good morning to you.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.656
What we're talking about

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.525
is during a really tough winter

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.393
that's coming up having been in Europe

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.561
and especially in Ukraine

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.630
during the wintertime, it is cold.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.031
So you're talking a combination

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.400
of not only electricity, but heat,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.736
any kind of power supplies.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.738
It would not only contribute

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.305
to the support

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.540
of the civilian population,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.241
but also support of the military.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.644
So it is certainly an approach

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.778
that the Russians have used

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.712
from the very beginning,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.314
taking away the infrastructure.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.082
But it's going to be

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.650
particularly important

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.018
during this period of the year.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.188
What can Ukraine and

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.522
its allies in the West

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.990
realistically do to either

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.159
prevent that or try to circumvent

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.662
some of the effects it causes?

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.130
Well,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:37.664
they've been doing

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.731
quite a bit in terms

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.732
of providing air

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:44.170
defense support capabilities to destroy

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.939
incoming missiles and rockets

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.674
that that the Soviets are using.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.776
And now a drones that they've received

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.377
received from Iran.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.848
So it is all part of the counteroffensive

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.683
that Ukraine is conducting.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.084
Unfortunately,

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.120
the Russians have fired so many

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.390
missiles, rockets, drones at all

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.025
different types of targets

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.328
in a very large area of Ukraine.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.730
There's no pinpointed target.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.032
So Ukraine has to defend everywhere,

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.534
and that's virtually impossible,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.069
even though they've been very successful

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.204
in knocking down the majority.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.540
The vast majority of the incoming rounds.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.908
They haven't been able to knock down

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:22.242
all of them.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.676
And those are the ones that

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.478
unfortunately affect the power stations.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:26.713
While the

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.348
counteroffensive is making progress,

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.350
in some parts of eastern Ukraine,

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.385
they've hit snags in other parts

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.721
with these new Russian conscripts,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.423
as well as just muddy conditions.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:37.891
As you noted,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.260
we're starting to get into winter

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.327
or closer to winter.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.164
And the field, the landscape

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.966
is difficult for movement.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.701
What do you make of the new developments

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.537
in that part of Ukraine?

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.538
Yeah, it's interesting, Boris.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.705
I was just having a conversation

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.840
with a colleague about that.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.574
Those who draw

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.076
big circles and arrows on maps

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.346
forget that those map, those arrows

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.681
sometimes have to go through

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.616
swamps and lands

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.618
that are bogged down in places

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.453
where there is no roads and forest.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.388
So it's a whole lot easier

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.923
to draw those areas,

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:10.723
those arrows,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.458
than it is to actually maneuver

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.760
in those locations.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.762
But Ukraine has done a very good job.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:16.429
Yes.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.697
Russia is

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.832
basically stacking their defenses

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.468
with a new mobile as mobilized recruits.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:23.636
But again,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.172
those recruits are absolutely untrained.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.174
Terrible and joining units

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.342
with low morale.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.377
So what we're seeing really is

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.312
Russia feeding

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.380
more meat to a meat grinder.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.481
And Russia,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.984
Ukraine will have increased challenges

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:38.985
with countering

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.920
those kinds of larger units, because,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.722
after all, quantity has a quality

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.656
all of its own.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.625
But I think because of the capability of

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:48.261
Ukraine's army, they will eventually win.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.028
They'll down.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:49.862
One of the areas

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.831
is that southern area person

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:52.432
estimates

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.000
by the Ukrainian intelligence is

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.369
that there are close to 40,000

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:57.537
Russian troops

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:58.571
on the

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.540
western bank of the river

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.375
that have no means to escape.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.610
So that's an area

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.912
that I'm I've been watching very closely

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.680
When you don't have the ability

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.448
to resupply,

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.550
soldiers have them escape or withdraw.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.951
It's going to be very difficult.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.486
And there is the huge potential

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.588
for Ukraine to capture

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.023
a great many of those soldiers

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:19.592
and take them completely out of action.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.294
Feeding meat to a meat grinder.

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.429
Wow. That's that's tough.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.865
Notably, there have been indications

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:26.866
from both

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.702
Republicans and Democrats in Congress

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.105
that there are doubts about maintaining

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.339
the level of support

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.608
for Ukraine that we've seen thus far.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.378
Are you concerned with what support

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.446
for Ukraine might look like after

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.381
the midterm elections

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.950
going into a new Congress next year?

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.951
Yeah, I am, Boris.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.685
I'm concerned

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:46.719
about the narrative

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.054
that some are presenting

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.455
in terms of this case.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.523
What you're talking about

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.124
is a nation

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.825
that's fighting for its sovereignty

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.494
and for its independence.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.229
The West has supported Ukraine

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.331
very well so far. They're increasing.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.533
The president just gave another package

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.202
of $725 million to Ukraine

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.071
just in the last few days.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.339
What we're talking about

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.540
is the potential

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.742
for the United States

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.911
and NATO, truthfully, to be affected

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.781
by inflationary

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.249
prices based on

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.051
what's been happening in Ukraine,

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.385
but also kind of

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.688
an overwhelming information

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.222
flow that we see sometimes.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.258
And the public gets tired of

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.626
and there's a fatigue.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.227
But we have to remember,

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.329
Ukrainian citizens

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.763
are fighting for their freedom,

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:31.998
for their sovereignty.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.766
And we have always presented

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.935
our American values to other nations.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.870
When you're doing that, in this case,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.872
going against a Russian force

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.641
that actually is committing

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.608
multiple

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:43.443
war crimes,

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.044
and we'll either get you

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.479
illegal activity,

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.580
what you're talking about

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.415
is really having an attempt

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.683
to sustain that through

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.452
what's going to be a very tough winter.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.487
I'm convinced that we will do that.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.189
But it will certainly come up

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.657
in a debate in Congress

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.058
and in NATO's as well.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.259
But the support seems to

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:01.260
continue to flow.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.830
General Hertling, as

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.164
always, appreciate your expertize.

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.467
Thanks. Pleasure, Bruce. Thank you.

